# Aim 2 Medication Assistant - environment configuration (EXAMPLE / PLACEHOLDER)
# Copy to ".env" and fill in for your environment. Do NOT commit a real ".env".
#
# SYNTHETIC DATA ONLY. None of these settings authorise real patient data.
# Serving real PHI requires IRB + HIPAA/CITI sign-off first (see
# NEEDS_PI_SIGNOFF.md). These knobs do not change that gate.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With nothing set, the app runs exactly as the
# local demo did: 127.0.0.1:8000 over plain HTTP.

# ---- Local development (defaults shown; leave unset to use them) ----
# ASM_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ASM_PORT=8000

# ---- Deployment (uncomment & set when you actually deploy) ----

# Bind on all interfaces so a reverse proxy / the network can reach the app:
# ASM_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Public address users type. Used to build shareable survey links. Set to your
# real domain once you have one:
# ASM_PUBLIC_URL=https://asm.example.org          # TODO: your domain

# You are running behind nginx/Caddy/Traefik that terminates TLS and forwards
# X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Forwarded-Host:
# ASM_BEHIND_PROXY=1

# Send the session cookie only over HTTPS. REQUIRED once you have TLS;
# keep OFF for plain-HTTP local use or the browser will drop the cookie:
# ASM_COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Stable signing secret for session cookies + CSRF. Without it the app falls
# back to a random key persisted on disk (fine locally, but it resets on every
# container rebuild). Generate one:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# ASM_SECRET=                                      # TODO: paste a long random value

# First-run doctor password (otherwise a random one is printed at startup and
# must be changed in-app). Change it after first login regardless:
# ASM_DOCTOR_PASSWORD=                             # TODO: set, then rotate in-app

# Database file location (defaults to ./clinic_data/clinic.db). Point at a
# persistent volume in a container so data survives restarts:
# ASM_DB=/data/clinic.db
